{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-014-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Rendering/OutlierClassifierTests.cs","line":322,"method":"OutlierClassifier_Cluster_FlagsSection_When25PercentRejected","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Rendering/OutlierClassifier.cs:302; remove the mask |= Cluster line -> red while the test-side rate guard holds","what_it_asserts":"unconditionally only RejectedCount>=1; the Cluster-bit assertion is wrapped in if (flags.RejectedCount > flags.SampleCount * 0.20), a test-side recompute of the production rate gate","why_weak":"the named contract (Cluster bit at >20 percent) self-disables whenever a threshold or classifier change lowers the rejection count, leaving a test that can no longer fail for its stated reason","proposed_action":"assert the rejected count reaches the expected 4 of 16 unconditionally, then assert the Cluster bit unconditionally; add a mirror case just under the rate (3 of 16) asserting the bit is clear","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-014-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Rendering/OutlierClassifierTests.cs","line":385,"method":"OutlierClassifier_HR1_DoesNotMutateRecording","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Rendering/OutlierClassifier.cs:210; write a mutated TrajectoryPoint back into section.frames[0] inside the per-sample loop -> red; the same write at frames[3] stays green","what_it_asserts":"reference identity of Points / TrackSections / frames, the frame count, and frames[0].ut","why_weak":"HR-1 is a whole-payload read-only invariant but only sample 0's ut is value-checked, so an in-place rewrite of any interior sample (exactly what a future write-back of rejection state would do) leaves the gate green","proposed_action":"snapshot every frame's ut/lat/lon/alt/velocity before Classify and compare the full list afterwards","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
